<title>ROMANIA: Blizzards disrupt Romanian transport.</title>
<headline>Blizzards disrupt Romanian transport.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blizzards swept across Romania on Thursday disrupting road and rail transport and shipping on the river Danube and in the Black sea, the Transport Ministry said.</p>
<p>Bucharest's Otopeni international airport remained operational, a ministry official said.</p>
<p>Snow disrupted rail traffic between the capital city and the country's main Black Sea port of Constanta, with trains halted or delayed by drifting, he said.</p>
<p>The River Danube port of Sulina and Galati had been shut by the bad weather, the official said, adding that gales had shut Constanta to shipping since 3 a.m. (0100 GMT).</p>
<p>Traffic on roads in eastern Romania was blocked by heavy snow bringing freight traffic to a halt in the area and forcing many motorists to abandon their cars, the private television station Media Pro said.</p>
<p>The outlook for the next few days was for unstable and cold weather.</p>
</text>
